WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.980
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:26.700
You're a <i>yokai</i> and yet you help humans.
What are you up to?

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.170
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.230
I didn't see! I didn't see them!

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.920
That has to be an illusion!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.550
Aren't you being a little cold?

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:34.310
I come here every night.
Are you going to ignore me again?

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.370
Play some Cat's Cradle with me.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.930
How about a game of <i>Sugoroku</i>?

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.320
CHAPTER 23

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.260
THE <i>YOKAI</i> APARTMENT SECRET STORY

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.780
Thank you very much.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.670
NAGATOMI MOVERS

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.630
LEAVE MOVING TO US!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.910
What? Working on your day off?!

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.210
But you promised!

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:45.500
I just sent all the clothes and the bed!

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:50.440
If you're not there, the movers can't
get into the new place, Hiro-kun!

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.760
HIRO-KUN
CALL ENDED

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.520
I was hoping to relax a bit.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.450
<i>SOKAI</i> LIVELY APARTMENT

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.520
I guess I'll have to
open the place for them.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.710
Hurry, hurry!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.880
I'll have to catch a cab.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.180
Oh well.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.040
Who's there?

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.420
I'm in a bit of a rush.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.790
We hear you're tearing this place down
to make a parking lot.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:31.050
Would you please be
willing to reconsider, Natsumi-san?

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.990
You know my name?

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.300
Who are you?

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:38.300
Could you at least hear us out,
Natsumi-san?

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:39.810
Huh?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.060
THE YEAR 1968

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.110
I wonder what sort of tenants we'll have?

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.320
From today,
this is <i>Sokai</i> Lively Apartment!

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.990
No matter who comes, everyone who
lives here is our family!

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:02.750
Let's be wonderful landlords, Haruo-san.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.330
Of course, Fuyuko-san.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.420
-Haruo-san!
-Fuyuko-san!

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.730
-Haruo-san!!
-Fuyuko-san!!

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.140
H-Hold it right there!

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.130
Yes?

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.640
By "Haruo" and "Fuyuko,"
you mean Grandpa and Grandma?

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.680
Yes.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.060
You said you'd take care of the key,

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.400
and that you just wanted to talk,
so I believed you.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.240
Monsters looking down from the window?

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.530
Am I an idiot?
Or just completely gullible?

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:38.800
Not monsters, <i>yokai</i>.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.810
Oh, <i>yokai</i>!

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.370
Could you leave after all?

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.460
Catchick will handle the key.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:53.090
Please hear us out.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.720
Okay...

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.900
What is with this apartment?!

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.780
No one said there were ghosts here!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.780
I thought the rent was suspiciously low!

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:20.340
We're leaving!

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:23.030
We're very sorry.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:30.060
At this rate there won't be
anyone to rent rooms from us.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.670
Haruo-san?

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.740
Please, I'm begging you! Go away!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.100
ROKURO-KUBI

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:50.690
Why? I'm just a harmless <i>yokai</i>
whose neck stretches.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.070
AKANAME

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.880
This one just licks grime from baths.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.700
I'm useful on rainy days.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.330
KARAKASA

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.660
That's not the issue!

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:09.580
Besides, <i>yokai</i> aren't supposed to
haunt newly built apartments!

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.790
What about someplace older...

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.460
Well, it's facing the wrong way
for one thing.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.280
Plus, this place used to be a graveyard.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.970
The Shinto alter location is
just the worst.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.100
<i>YOKAI</i> APARTMENT

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.600
<i>Evil spirits begone!</i>

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.690
My work is done.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.190
Um, they're still...

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.380
Huh?

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.300
Can't you see them?

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.660
Uh...

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.160
You don't give up, do you?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.750
In an age where people have gone to space

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:56.790
and we've got premade instant curry,
talking about ghosts is a bit much.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:02.050
They only show up when it's convenient,

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:05.140
and normally
they keep themselves invisible!

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:09.370
That's just superstition. Go home.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.400
Seriously?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.280
He was at school bragging about it today.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.070
Then let's check out this Yokai Mailbox.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:27.540
Don't you wanna see if this Kitaro's
<i>yokai</i> extermination is true or not?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.850
Guys!

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:35.340
My mom said we can watch
<i>The Great Yokai Space War</i> at my place!

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.050
Awesome!

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.230
You kids...

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.640
TO KITARO

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.350
Is this <i>Sokai</i> Lively Apartment?

00:08:58.360 --> 00:08:59.610
Yes!

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:02.920
Thank you so much for coming!

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.370
This is ridiculous.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:06.470
What?

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.410
How old are you right now?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.910
I've never counted.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.460
Besides, <i>yokai</i> don't even exist.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:17.650
It turns out they do.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.110
Huh?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.400
Hm?

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:27.930
You can't just pop out like that.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.620
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:34.140
<i>YOKAI</i> APARTMENT

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.650
<i>YOKAI</i> AKANAME

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:37.580
-<i>"Eek!"</i>
-<i>"What?"</i>

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.580
<i>"Scratch, scratch."</i>

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:49.600
You're a <i>yokai</i> and yet you help humans.
What are you up to?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.020
You need a little disciplining.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.390
Get him!

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.090
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.180
Got you!

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.600
Take this!

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.990
Thank you, Kitaro-kun!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:26.950
Would you like something to eat?
It should hit the spot!

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:28.970
I'll whip something up now.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.370
I wanna stay here!

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:38.000
You don't find dank, dreary and
comfortable homes like this every day.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.230
The bath had the best grime
for this one to lick...

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.720
Akaname, Rokuro-Kubi, Karakasa.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.080
Humans and <i>yokai</i> can't be allowed
to get too close.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.930
Being feared is the perfect distance.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.710
Um...

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.780
THE YEAR 1971
(JAPAN-WIDE BOWLING BOOM)

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:08.570
<i>BiBiBi no Bi</i>

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:18.040
Yum! No wonder these cost as much
as two red bean buns and a bottle of milk.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.690
Not bad!

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:23.360
I should find enough loose change
to buy another.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:29.220
Thanks for waiting until
I had enough for rent.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.550
We all help each other when in need.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.800
<i>The temple grounds are already filled
with people here for New Year's...</i>

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.580
Happy New Year.

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:41.440
We made it through another year.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.150
Indeed.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:45.820
All the tenants are lively.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.820
Our daughter's lively.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:51.340
It's been a year of
nothing but good things.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:58.310
It might all be the <i>yokai</i> repaying us.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.590
<i>Grandpa and Grandma didn't</i>
<i>drive the </i>yokai<i> out?!</i>

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:04.420
<i>No.</i>

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.890
<i>"Don't tease humans or show yourselves."</i>

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:15.240
-<i>That was the deal.</i>
-Beer... Beer...

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.100
<i>Whoa, whoa, whoa! Why?!</i>

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:24.360
Aki-chan, there are <i>yokai</i>
living in this apartment.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.030
Do you think she'll be able to see them?

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.280
Who knows?

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:33.590
But everyone who lives here
is part of our family.

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.820
THE YEAR 1985

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.740
I'm so successful it's crazy!

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.540
Have this! Hah!

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:55.050
Why? How?!

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:59.760
My, my. Accidents are certainly scary.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:06.660
We won't bow to land sharks!
We'll never leave this property!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.650
Land shark is a little rude.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:13.300
Oh? Your daughter is certainly pretty.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.640
I'll be back in three days.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:30.800
I've had it! Why do Dad and Mom
care so much about this apartment?!

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:33.550
I don't think we can hold out any longer.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.180
You're right.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.180
There's her entrance exam to consider.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.930
You're right.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.680
Everyone will understand...

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.210
Excuse me.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:54.650
It's been a while.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:14:00.200
We don't intend to
get involved with human affairs.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:04.290
But we can't ignore something
that affects fellow <i>yokai</i>.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:15.630
These <i>yakuza</i> have
a tacky sense of style.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.660
Who are those guys?!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.390
Ow!

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:23.600
What the hell?!

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:44.790
How can we thank you?

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:49.130
Forget it, I'm blushing. Besides,
Kitaro and the others did all the work.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.000
You know what they say.

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:56.010
"A landlord is like a parent
and a tenant is like a child."

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.260
Right?

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:02.030
Please stay here as long as you like.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.270
And there you have it.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:14.490
Would you be willing to reconsider
tearing down this apartment?

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:18.700
Hmm. Even if that's all true,

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:22.620
no one's rented here for a long time.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:23.850
Besides...

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.040
Hiro-kun!

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.540
Yeah, I'll take care of it quickly.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.310
Huh? <i>Yokai</i>?

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:32.980
I'll see you later.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.760
Hiro-kun!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.510
Natsumi, I took care of work
at Mach speed for you.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:42.140
Really? You're so wonderful!

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:43.840
Huh? Who are they?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.300
Oh, don't worry about them.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.770
This is my fiancé, Hiro-kun.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.250
We're going to live together
in our new place.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.880
So, sorry about this!

00:15:55.460 --> 00:16:00.420
We'll have to move Rokuro-Kubi and
the others to GeGeGe Forest.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:03.780
That tacky jacket...

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:04.620
Huh?

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:07.620
I've seen it somewhere...

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:11.690
Give it back! Please give it back!

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.380
Got the deed and the registered seal.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.300
Why, Hiro-kun?

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:23.550
Gimme a break.
Surely you had your suspicions.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:27.310
What kind of real estate agent
wears a jacket like this?!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.310
How could you trick me?

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.060
How cruel...

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:36.610
You knew I was tricking you,
but you still couldn't leave me.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:37.940
Right?

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:38.880
Huh?

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:46.260
If it worked I could sell this
to some eccentric buyer.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.240
No... Don't touch it...

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:53.130
Poor little girl.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:56.590
You lost your mom as a child,

00:16:56.590 --> 00:17:00.010
and your grandfather who raised you
just died recently.

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.360
Stop it...

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:07.760
Sad, lonely girls are
the easiest ones to trick.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.450
Later!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.520
Crummy old apartment.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:17.610
Where are you going?

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:18.810
Huh?

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:34.910
You're sure about that?!

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:41.110
The tacky taste. His jacket was a Versachu
just like the one that land shark wore!

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.250
Maybe I'm being punished.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:18:01.320
I tried to tear down Grandpa's apartment
and drive you all out.

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:07.430
It's punishment...

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:18.850
I know...

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.760
I know you.

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.300
But how?

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:33.260
Spacewalk time!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.230
Here's a broom.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:46.530
-This way!
-Wait for me!

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.650
It's a real help.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:52.720
She's had it rough,
so she needs lots of friends.

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:56.350
Sand Witch-san?

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:01.960
She prefers playing with <i>yokai</i>
over the neighborhood kids?

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:06.190
Really? Natsumi said that?

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:10.140
Okay! We'll keep playing with her and--

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:11.260
-Idiot!
-Huh?

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:13.060
Natsumi's a human.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:17.200
What will you do if she can't
live a normal human life anymore?!

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:19.820
Oh.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:23.130
But what are we supposed to do about it?

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:30.150
Akaname, Rokuro-Kubi, Karakasa?
Where are you?

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:35.120
Come here, Natsumi.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.370
Grandpa...

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.560
Grandpa!

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:44.420
